CREOracle role isolation
├── when initializing an oracle
│   ├── it grants configured admin, guard and limits roles independently of ownership
│   ├── it requires an explicit operational role even for the owner and admin
│   ├── it leaves zero role holders unassigned even with a nonzero owner
│   ├── it grants configured roles even with a zero owner
│   ├── it preserves full movement-limit precision and accepts the one-million maximum
│   ├── it rejects values above one million atomically before narrowing full-width inputs
│   └── it exposes ERC165, receiver, access-control and enumerable-role interfaces
├── when the account grants matching roles or its default admin role
│   └── it does not authorize oracle operations or oracle role administration
├── when granting and revoking oracle roles
│   ├── it enforces separate guard and limits roles
│   ├── it ignores account role revocation when an oracle role is still granted
│   ├── it enforces oracle revocation even while the matching account role remains granted
│   └── it isolates grants and revocations from other oracle instances
├── when transferring ownership and role administration
│   ├── it keeps existing oracle roles until explicitly changed
│   └── it enumerates the new oracle admin without changing account roles
└── when migrating the oracle
    └── it preserves local role memberships, enumeration and operational authority
